  "qualification": "Each query begins with the same float64 array of 256 input samples and returns 256 output values. Both methods use the first five validation inputs, one untimed call and five timed calls per input; the reported cost is the median of the five per-input medians. FNO timing includes float32 conversion and prediction; Euler timing includes restriction to its internal grid, initial-value copying, any sparse factorization, all timesteps, and periodic linear output interpolation. Model loading, imports and reference-error calculations are excluded. The selected classical candidate is the fastest among the two Euler methods at internal n=64,128,256 whose mean error on all 40 validation examples is no larger than the FNO mean. Setup includes training and validation label generation plus training/checkpoint selection; it excludes test labels, numerical refinement checks, benchmark calibration, and post-training diagnostics."
